Enhancement: Reload the page after a theme app is enabled or disabled

A theme only takes effect with the next page load: the header, the logo and
the colours come with the page from the server. After enabling or disabling a
theme app on the Apps page of the admin settings, the admin kept seeing the
old appearance until reloading the page by hand. The page now announces
"Updating the appearance …" and reloads after one and a half seconds, or right
away when the message is confirmed.

Other apps are not affected. A theme that still needs an update keeps the
existing redirect to the update page, so the page reloads only once.
